---
layout: layouts/default.njk
title: The Bulletin
summary: Keith Dunstan's articles published in The Bulletin.
---

<div class="row">
  <div class="col-12 col-lg-8 offset-lg-2">
    <p class="lead">Keith Dunstan wrote in The Bulletin from 1962 until 1984, initially under the psuedonym, 'Batman'.</p>
<p><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Bulletin_(Australian_periodical)">"The Bulletin"</a> magazine shaped how Australian identity, literature and public debate were understood and represented. Through early writers such as Henry Lawson and Banjo Paterson, it gave prominence to a distinctive national literary voice and helped popularise the bush myth: an influential but limited story of independence, mateship and life beyond the city. </p><p>Prior to its last edition in 2008, The Bulletin was also important as a record of the cultural values and social attitudes of its time, including the exclusions and assumptions that shaped public conversation. Its development from a politically charged publication into a modern news magazine showed how Australian media changed over time.</P
    <h4>Articles</h4>
    {% set decades = collections.bulletin | groupByDecade %}
    <div class="accordion pt-3 pb-3" id="bulletinAccordion">
      {% for group in decades %}
        <div class="accordion-item">
          <h2 class="accordion-header" id="heading{{ group.decade }}">
            <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapse{{ group.decade }}" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapse{{ group.decade }}">
              {{ group.decade }}s
              <span class="ms-auto me-2 text-muted">{{ group.articles.length }} article{{ "s" if group.articles.length != 1 }}</span>
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="collapse{{ group.decade }}" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="heading{{ group.decade }}" data-bs-parent="#bulletinAccordion">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <ul class="list-unstyled mb-0">
                {% for article in group.articles %}
                  <li class="mb-2">
                    <a href="{{ article.url | url }}">{{ article.data.title }}</a>
                    <span class="text-muted"> — {{ article.date | readableDate }}</span>
                  </li>
                {% endfor %}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% else %}
        <p>No Bulletin articles found yet.</p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
